{"doc_id": "doc28575", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "In Western culture, the white stork is famously associated with delivering babies to new parents, a symbolism rooted in European folklore. This legend, though ancient, gained widespread popularity through a 19th-century story by Hans Christian Andersen titled \"The Storks.\" German traditions specifically suggested storks would find infants in caves or marshes, transporting them via a basket carried on their backs or held in their beaks, with the belief in \"stork stones\" within those caves. Alternatively, babies might be deposited down the chimney. Households wishing for children were said to show their desire by offering sweets on the window sill for the stork. This symbolism has since spread globally, reaching places like the Philippines and South American nations. Furthermore, a common red birthmark on the back of newborns' heads, known as nevus flammeus nuchae, is occasionally called a stork-bite.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 81349774, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "The white stork, a bird central to European folklore, is traditionally believed to bring babies to new parents. This legend, popularised by a 19th-century Hans Christian Andersen story, held in some German traditions that storks found infants in caves or marshes, identified by 'stork stones', and transported them to households, sometimes via a basket or beak, or even down the chimney. Households wishing for children were said to signal their desire by offering sweets to the stork. The symbolism of the white stork delivering newborns has since spread beyond Europe to places like the Philippines and South America. This connection is also reflected in the medical term for a specific birthmark, nevus flammeus nuchae, sometimes called a stork-bite mark.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 2071177846, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "f98807b437cd8dca514c940f6341902e50fbafec2d936c55d5d479e9477b2719", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "bringing babies to new parents", "matched_aliases": ["bringing babies to new parents"], "query_id": "test802", "question_hash": "3e4113be7cc16dcfa55ce917f18d0019cb00df2ff7eb508fb18a8d46f39d4b7e", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 0, "row_hash": "57f22c64e9e5417e67ab60a69a9cc8ec0cec9b368e245c76f21bdcd21c26f719", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1339973140, "similarity": 0.07439553626782393, "source_content_hash": "b604911c11205e81ce26875bd53423faa6ca1fc4b160388b94130b61fd85d29a", "source_hash": "ca39c0e544a127056fb4ca8a16dd9583d32c5b4ca74ff1f1f24c63c2924e2d1d", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.7, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "6274bd0e507959da34feff90acbaff121f284de6520a2a140c0aa6185d92f324", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d93996298f", "version": "v2"}, "validation_goal": "query_answerability"}}
{"doc_id": "doc28685", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "In contract bridge, honors can be declared at any point following the auction, before the play concludes. This declaration is typically made by the player holding the honors, usually at the end of a trick or immediately after the final card is played, to ensure the opponents are aware of the score. The strategic timing is often delayed until the play finishes to prevent opponents from gaining insights into the card distribution based on the honors called prematurely. Remember, honors can belong to any player, including the dummy.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1060408398, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "bb973839786d5d10ed5deb561285018d028cb2671b0a6bd86346a982fc70cb6e", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "any time after the auction", "matched_aliases": ["any time after the auction"], "query_id": "test804", "question_hash": "b995b4df2988a707b969a1c1f596799a903c2aa29e2fde006a7c40cf4ef8941c", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 0, "row_hash": "1dead84718343b0c004a8891087bde44c698ff7b68f6f1718d6771f90a479e92", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 199177281, "similarity": 0.034108527131782945, "source_content_hash": "65b15f3463186dbcce558327b8f0c4942f556ddbdc54750d879df77ba41c0ba8", "source_hash": "a35621f0d123ad17f3e5a0633fe97d170772f12c66be23a34323dcadc16cab11", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "f739a165deaf8dfa04f4c3abf49e103a040796aed6a8f372a2aa106b32a13d47", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": false, "stage": "correct_generation", "validation_goal": "query_answerability", "validator_hash": "a02bd2beee5a12b1acaa721f9e5fc6aa8fe87d0fc104e403231550d