{"doc_id": "doc37187", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "On March 11, 2013, Lucasfilm announced that Star Wars: The Clone Wars series would conclude, effectively ending its contract with Cartoon Network after Disney's acquisition. This cancellation prompted the release of previously unreleased episodes, known as \"bonus content,\" which were later confirmed by Super RTL to be broadcast as a sixth season. This final season, comprising 13 episodes, was made available on Netflix beginning March 7, 2014.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 55743215, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "On March 11, 2013, Lucasfilm announced that Star Wars: The Clone Wars series would be concluding, effectively canceling its ongoing run with Cartoon Network after Disney's acquisition. However, this decision impacted the planned continuation. Separately, on January 16, 2014, the German network Super RTL declared their intention to release the existing, unreleased bonus content episodes as a sixth season, totaling thirteen installments. Furthermore, Lucasfilm confirmed that this sixth season, alongside previous seasons and the feature film, would be distributed on Netflix, becoming available on March 7, 2014.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1550546781, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "23db6ce8c98e17d451f135aaa0ca6c189a25a78055e9fef6c4838c3e854521c3", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "6", "matched_aliases": ["6", "six"], "query_id": "test1068", "question_hash": "198845dcb13f881329e0f51a592262ae7d3b4272944d0a5cd0a9e88bdfaba836", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 0, "row_hash": "3bddcf740495c00f475e6333bf4ccc90fe0e294bb2df894f80008737b61edced", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 1969243287, "similarity": 0.4563758389261745, "source_content_hash": "1352ef7e4e5f9553624f710921a40baba3baea