{"doc_id": "doc46266", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Cadillac Mountain, located in Acadia National Park, is renowned for being the place where the first sunrise in the United States occurs. This happens specifically during the fall and winter months, when the sun rises over its summit while positioned south of due east.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 722290048, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}, {"attempt": 2, "generated_text": "Cadillac Mountain, a notable peak within Acadia National Park, is famously recognized as the place where the first sunrise occurs in the United States during the fall and winter months. This location attracts many visitors hoping to witness the initial light of day. However, it's important to note that the summit only claims this distinction in fall and winter, when the sun rises south of due east. During most of spring and summer, the earliest sunrise is observed elsewhere, specifically at Mars Hill, located 150 miles northeast of Cadillac. For a brief period around the equinoxes, the first sunrise occurs even further east, at West Quoddy Head in Lubec, Maine.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1372863430, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.5}], "fingerprint": "7cd8c4123e93869a18eabfa7d6567f596f5b09f5690afaa21466047e42c35acd", "generation_attempts": 3, "gold_answer": "the summit of Cadillac Mountain", "matched_aliases": ["the summit of Cadillac Mountain"], "query_id": "test1305", "question_hash": "8e467f43c7b1b01696db3ec61d083c5eb13ef2a858cedc2acf54cf7775fe2732", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 0, "row_hash": "3c212cb6f85d9464e86e05b7faa5243a7d7629d1f0e63cc3819e1f4ddbbe17f5", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 357836946, "similarity": 0.025069637883008356, "source_content_hash": "4c02fe78c05ea976159be8730cb4221e7f01d49f1a10815e804cd1145a1924df", "source_hash": "b339087cbb6ee168d21731b1c8