{"doc_id": "doc48413", "receipt": {"answer_in_original_body": true, "failed_attempts": [{"attempt": 1, "generated_text": "Vertebrates, organisms characterized by the presence of a backbone or spinal column, are thought to have first appeared on Earth roughly 525 million years ago, emerging alongside a vast increase in other life forms during the Cambrian explosion. The earliest known example of a vertebrate is believed to be the genus Myllokunmingia. This ancient creature, along with its close relatives like Haikouichthys ercaicunensis, possessed fundamental vertebrate features including a notochord, rudimentary vertebrae, and a distinct head and tail region. These initial vertebrates lacked true jaws and primarily survived by filter-feeding near the ocean floor.", "reason": "missing_gold_answer", "seed": 1954797015, "similarity": null, "temperature": 0.3}], "fingerprint": "5670424df31a100eb41485c0ec4abe0df897555478775df490560a0288094e25", "generation_attempts": 2, "gold_answer": "believed to be the Myllokunmingia", "matched_aliases": ["believed to be the Myllokunmingia", "the Myllokunmingia"], "query_id": "test1370", "question_hash": "27c5679940a041d591fad8e68fa85655141fd6b75b706c8bfd0847421988298a", "repair_from": null, "replaced_row_hash": null, "replaced_text": null, "retry_seed": 0, "row_hash": "2d43a77d8b720b7e71a54ea22e932545da389d9264dc26522b26463bb9280070", "scope": "all_answer_documents", "seed": 969977166, "similarity": 0.12035398230088495, "source_content_hash": "81606ad53ddaa6d1164ec4f43cfa2ab7a020ea2260a29ae9d7c6434b7e3e4b50", "source_hash": "caa1c90f608c3ebb84d779bb88ddb329291dbcdcc86dbef9ff13aef97bd991e2", "target_answer": null, "temperature": 0.5, "validation": {"answerability_verified": false, "evidence_hash": "67f614fec179aa417f28d6f2463cbd441983cda1746c709b199c2824f17aa9ca", "format_attempts": [], "judgment": {"gold_alias_present": true, "not_near_duplicate": true}, "mode": "deterministic", "model": null, "provider": null, "semantic_verified": fa